{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the flesh and the skin.</b> Rashi explained: we find no outer sin-offering burned except this one and that of the inauguration offerings. And if you ask: but do we not find the second bull of the Levites in the portion בהעלותך, and in Ezra twelve goats of a sin-offering — all as an עולה לה׳ — and in Ezekiel a bull of a sin-offering for the future, all of which are outer sin-offerings and are burned? One may answer: the second bull in the portion בהעלותך was an inauguration offering, for they filled the hands of the Levites to enter into service; and also those in the days of Ezra and the bull of a sin-offering for the future are inauguration offerings, as the Master said: just as they offered in the days of Moses, so they offered in the days of Ezra, and so they are destined to offer in the future to come. And what Rashi explained here — 'and that of the inauguration offerings' — refers to all of them: to the bull of the sin-offering mentioned in the portion תצוה, and to the second bull of the Levites written in the portion בהעלותך, and to the twelve goats of a sin-offering for idolatry in the days of Ezra, and to the bull of a sin-offering of the future written in Ezekiel — for all of them are inauguration offerings. And in the first chapter of Horayot he resolves that those of Ezra were a special ruling for the hour." "<b>Burned in fire.</b> The reason has already been explained in the portion תצוה and in the portion צו."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:56.633490725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}